  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#43408\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before in PowerToys#43408 (HWiNFO showing a UAC prompt but never opening when launched from Command Palette, while Start Menu works). The cause identified there is that some apps cannot be elevated from the unelevated WinUI3 process: the launch fails with a Win32Exception ('No application is associated with the specified file') after the first UAC dialog. The ticket's discussion mentions a possible fix of bundling sudo or a similar helper to launch the elevation, but the ticket doesn't record a released fix. In the meantime, launch these apps from the Start Menu or directly from their .exe. Some users also see two entries for the same app in Command Palette, and one of them works, so try the other entry (e.g. a different shortcut for the same app). If it still fails on 0.100.2, add your details (LenovoLegionToolkit, HWiNFO64) to PowerToys#43408.\"}",
